From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: adaptive context checkpointing -- the checkpoints this
 track creates are restored exactly zero times (+2.4% score)

`llama-server` creates context checkpoints while evaluating a prompt for any
model whose memory cannot be partially rolled back (SWA, recurrent, hybrid).
Qwen3.6-35B-A3B is hybrid, so it pays in full. Two things are bought each time:

  * the prompt is deliberately BROKEN at `{4 + n_ubatch, 4}` tokens from its
    end (`checkpoint_offsets`, ref llama.cpp PR 20288) so the state can be
    captured before those tokens are evaluated -- the ranked 534-token prompt
    therefore runs as **three** `llama_decode` calls of 18 + 512 + 4;
  * `llama_state_seq_get_data` copies the whole sequence state on each break --
    **62.813 MiB per checkpoint, two per ranked request.**

A checkpoint can only ever pay for itself if a LATER request into the same slot
shares a prefix long enough to reach it. The ranked harness gives every request
a unique prefix (`Sources/runner/base.ts`: `ttft <session> <i>: ...`), so none
ever does.

**Census, `llama-server --verbosity 4`, one replica session (14 tasks):**

```
created context checkpoint  ... 19 of them, 62.813 MiB each
restored context checkpoint ...  0
erased invalidated ckpt     ...  0
found better prompt (cache) ...  0
```

**A restore rate of exactly zero, and note the erase rate is zero too.** That is
the reason 0021's waste signal from the sibling track does not transfer: since
0054 moves the checkpoint payloads into the prompt-cache entry instead of
deep-copying them, this server never logs `erased invalidated context
checkpoint` at all, so a credit driven by erases would never decrement and the
port would be structurally inert. The signal used here is the one that survives
0054: **a task created checkpoints and no restore ever followed.**

The patch replaces the unconditional `params_base.n_ctx_checkpoints > 0` gate
with that credit: creation is allowed while credit remains, a successful
restore refills it to 4, a task that created checkpoints without a restore
spends one, and after 64 dry tasks a single probe task is let through so
traffic that starts sharing prefixes turns the feature back on by itself.
Multi-turn chat, which restores checkpoints constantly, never loses the
feature. `LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT=0` restores stock behaviour and is the A/B toggle
used below.

Nothing about what the model computes changes in kind: a missing checkpoint
only ever means the prompt is re-evaluated from a shorter cached prefix, which
is precisely what stock already does whenever no checkpoint matches.

**Firing is proven structurally, from the server log, not from a clock**
(`--verbosity 4`, 14 tasks):

```
task  0 | created context checkpoint 1, 2      <- the credit, 2 tasks
task 11 | created context checkpoint 1, 2
task 22 | cached n_tokens = 0                  <- ONE llama_decode call
   (12 further tasks, zero checkpoints, one chunk each)
`cached n_tokens` lines: 18 over 14 tasks  =  2 x 3 + 12 x 1
```

so the ranked prompt goes from **three `llama_decode` calls to one**, and
`prompt cache update took` drops from 7.79-10.37 ms to 0.00-0.01 ms on the
tasks that no longer carry 125.6 MiB of checkpoint payload into the entry.

**Timing.** Same binary, env toggle, 8 arms interleaved
ctl/ck/pc/both/both/pc/ck/ctl x 9 measured runs, replica of
`Sources/runner/base.ts` with unique prompts (so every request is cache-cold
exactly as the ranked harness is):

| arm | TTFT | prefill tok/s | decode tok/s | minflt/ttft req | AnonHugePages |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| ctl | 0.16037 | 5350.6 | 161.47 | 891 | 5033984 kB |
| ck  | 0.14134 | 5537.1 | 162.18 | 267 | 2293760 kB |
| ck  | 0.14081 | 5596.9 | 161.47 | 333 | 2293760 kB |
| ctl | 0.16251 | 5230.7 | 161.01 | 840 | 5185536 kB |

Medians: **ttft 0.16144 -> 0.14108 (x1.1444), prefill 5290.6 -> 5567.0
(x1.0522), decode 161.24 -> 161.82 (x1.0036)**. The ttft arms are fully
disjoint. Retained huge-page state falls 5.03 GB -> 2.29 GB, which is the
125.6 MiB/request of checkpoint payload measured without a clock.

Cross-checked against a zero-rebuild probe on the frontier binary
(`--ctx-checkpoints 0`, 2 rounds): ttft 0.16155 -> 0.14080, prefill 5228.6 ->
5564.8, decode 161.87 -> 161.76. The adaptive form reaches the flag ceiling.

**Priced against this track's own score algebra, not the replica's.** With
`ttft = t(534)`, `prefill = (t(534)-t(84))/451`, `decode = (t_full-t(534))/127`
and the published frontier's numbers (0.19817 s, 0.14246 s, 0.78531 s):

```
dScore/Score = 1.3331*a + 0.8277*c - 1.4039*b     (a,b,c in seconds, saved on
                                                   the ttft / short / full req)
```

This patch measures **a = 20.4 ms, b = 16.1 ms, c = 23.2 ms**, i.e. the saving
lands on all three requests and slightly harder on the full one, which is why
decode does not pay for it here (it rose 0.36%). Ranked-priced: **+2.37%**, so
1.812930 -> ~1.856. The replica's own ratios model +3.28%; the smaller ranked
figure is the honest one, because the ranked harness has a 1.7x larger prefill
numerator and therefore values a fixed per-request saving less.

**Correctness.**

* **The gate binary is the same file.** Building the parent commit and the
  candidate and diffing the artefacts:

```
c787f9f16dfc419c329bab94a39b7121  bin/libggml-hip.so.0
32c1c78dd92e42814807c8bb667f067c  bin/libllama.so.0
852dda6479a47a9eaf45cdf87711b3bf  bin/llama-perplexity
c76719480218ce6def4fd0fae7f9507a  bin/libllama-common.so.0.0.10276
```

  identical on both arms; the change lives entirely in
  `libllama-server-impl.so`, which `llama-perplexity` does not load. The
  runner's gate command is therefore unaffected by construction, and the
  standing gate was re-drawn anyway (below).
* Runner's exact gate command, 3 loads per arm in one session: see the series
  README. The nondeterminism in this series is the 0008 pre-add fold and is
  unchanged by this patch.
* Served-path greedy identity: see the series README section for this round.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index a9d5b07cb..3f12834cc 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -963,6 +963,44 @@ private:
     int slots_debug = 0;
     int n_empty_consecutive = 0;
 
+    // [gainz] adaptive context checkpointing.
+    //
+    // For models whose memory cannot be partially rolled back (SWA, recurrent,
+    // hybrid -- Qwen3.6 is hybrid) the prompt loop creates context checkpoints
+    // while evaluating a prompt.  Each one costs an extra llama_decode call --
+    // the prompt is deliberately broken at {4 + n_ubatch, 4} tokens from its end
+    // purely so the state can be captured before those tokens are evaluated --
+    // plus a full llama_state_seq_get_data copy of the sequence state (62.81 MiB
+    // each on this model, two per 534-token request).
+    //
+    // A checkpoint only ever pays for itself if a LATER request into the same
+    // slot shares a prefix long enough to reach it.  When it does not, the whole
+    // cost was loss.  Note that with the checkpoint payloads moved into the
+    // prompt cache (see prompt_save/alloc consume) the server no longer logs
+    // "erased invalidated context checkpoint" at all, so the ONLY usable waste
+    // signal is "this task created checkpoints and no restore ever followed".
+    //
+    // The credit below makes creation self-tuning instead of unconditional: it
+    // is allowed while credit remains, a successful restore refills it, a task
+    // that created checkpoints without any restore spends one, and after a long
+    // dry spell a single probe task is let through so traffic that starts
+    // sharing prefixes turns the feature back on by itself.  Nothing about what
+    // the model computes changes -- a missing checkpoint only ever means the
+    // prompt is re-evaluated from a shorter cached prefix, which is exactly what
+    // stock already does whenever no checkpoint matches.
+    static constexpr int CKPT_CREDIT_MAX  = 4;
+    static constexpr int CKPT_PROBE_EVERY = 64;
+
+    bool ckpt_adaptive = [] {
+        const char * e = getenv("LLAMA_ADAPTIVE_CKPT");
+        return e == nullptr || atoi(e) != 0;
+    }();
+    int  ckpt_credit    = 2;
+    int  ckpt_idle      = 0;
+    int  ckpt_created   = 0;
+    bool ckpt_hit       = false;
+    int  ckpt_last_task = -1;
+
     std::unique_ptr<server_prompt_cache> prompt_cache;
 
     server_metrics metrics;
@@ -2390,6 +2428,9 @@ private:
         // stash the draft's speculative state with the checkpoint
         common_speculative_get_state(spec.get(), slot.id, cur.data_spec);
 
+        // [gainz] speculative work performed; only a later restore validates it
+        ckpt_created++;
+
         SLT_TRC(slot,
                 "created context checkpoint %d of %d (pos_min = %d, pos_max = %d, n_tokens = %" PRId64 ", size = %.3f MiB)\n",
                 (int) slot.prompt.checkpoints.size(), params_base.n_ctx_checkpoints, cur.pos_min,
@@ -3359,6 +3400,11 @@ private:
                                         // restore the draft's speculative state
                                         common_speculative_set_state(spec.get(), slot.id, it->data_spec);
 
+                                        // [gainz] a restore proves checkpoints are paying off on this traffic
+                                        ckpt_credit = CKPT_CREDIT_MAX;
+                                        ckpt_idle   = 0;
+                                        ckpt_hit    = true;
+
                                         pos_next = std::min(pos_next, std::max(it->pos_min + 1, it->pos_max));
                                         n_past   = std::min(slot.prompt.tokens.size_up_to_pos(pos_next), (size_t) it->n_tokens);
                                         SLT_TRC(slot, "restored context checkpoint (pos_min = %d, pos_max = %d, n_tokens = %" PRId64 ", n_past = %d, size = %.3f MiB)\n", it->pos_min, it->pos_max, it->n_tokens, n_past, (float) it->size() / 1024 / 1024);
@@ -3445,6 +3491,32 @@ private:
 
                     bool do_checkpoint = params_base.n_ctx_checkpoints > 0;
 
+                    // [gainz] adaptive context checkpointing -- see ckpt_credit above.
+                    // Settled once per task, before the first chunk of its prompt is
+                    // assembled, so every chunk of one prompt makes the same decision.
+                    if (ckpt_adaptive) {
+                        if (ckpt_last_task != slot.task->id) {
+                            ckpt_last_task = slot.task->id;
+
+                            if (ckpt_hit) {
+                                // a restore already refilled the credit
+                                ckpt_hit = false;
+                            } else if (ckpt_created > 0 && ckpt_credit > 0) {
+                                // created, never restored
+                                ckpt_credit--;
+                            }
+
+                            ckpt_created = 0;
+
+                            if (ckpt_credit == 0 && ++ckpt_idle >= CKPT_PROBE_EVERY) {
+                                ckpt_credit = 1;
+                                ckpt_idle   = 0;
+                            }
+                        }
+
+                        do_checkpoint = do_checkpoint && ckpt_credit > 0;
+                    }
+
                     // make checkpoints only for completion tasks
                     do_checkpoint = do_checkpoint && slot.task->type == SERVER_TASK_TYPE_COMPLETION;
 
